"""Direct answers to the two source-linked questions for each concept.

These lead with the requested answer before the longer teaching explanation.
"""
ANSWERS={
 'oscillation':('**Inertia carries the mass past equilibrium**, while the spring repeatedly restores it toward the middle. Those opposing tendencies create the cycle.','A return tendency alone does not explain **continued motion through equilibrium**. The moving mass’s inertia is also needed.'),
 'directions':('Both arrangements combine **a restoring force with inertia**. Changing the direction in which displacement is drawn does not remove that interaction.','The geometry changes from motion along the system to motion across it. **Restoring action and overshoot remain shared**.'),
 'mass-stiffness':('**Greater inertia slows reversal, while stronger restoring force speeds it up**. That is why mass and stiffness have opposite directional effects when the other properties stay fixed.','Changing more than one relevant property can produce competing effects. **The controlled comparison must identify what was held fixed** before one directional rule is applied.'),
 'two-modes':('In the lower mode the masses move together, while in the higher mode they oppose one another. **These are different patterns of the whole system**.','Opposite movement stretches the middle coupling more. **The extra restoring action raises the frequency** relative to shared-direction movement.'),
 'three-modes':('The first mode has broad shared motion, the second leaves the middle mass still, and the third alternates neighboring directions. **Each pattern has its own frequency**.','**The middle mass has no displacement in Mode 2**. Adding inertia there therefore does not change that mode’s motion in the ideal symmetric system.'),
 'many-modes':('An additional independently moving mass adds another degree of freedom. **The one-direction model therefore gains another independent normal mode**.','The limit spreads moving material and elastic coupling continuously along the string. **Many discrete patterns become a sequence of continuous-medium modes**.'),
 'fixed-fixed':('**Both endpoints must remain displacement nodes**. Whole numbers of half-waves fit those two conditions.','More half-waves in the same length give shorter wavelengths. At fixed wave speed, **the frequencies become whole-number multiples of the fundamental**.'),
 'membrane':('The membrane can support several organized spatial patterns at once. **Their contributions add into the overall motion**.','The point records the components that move there, and the spectrum separates their frequencies. **A pickup at a component’s node can miss its motion**.'),
 'scientific-method':('Record a periodic voice and measure the distances between spectral peaks. **Regular harmonic spacing is the observable prediction**.','The theory proposes the mechanism, the prediction states the expected pattern, and the measurement checks that pattern. **A test needs the connection among all three**.'),
 'fixed-free':('Odd counts connect a still end to a maximally moving end. **An even quarter-wave count would end at the wrong displacement condition**.','Both comparisons have **one constrained end and one free end**. That relationship transfers even though the physical materials and motion directions differ.'),
 'local-change':('A local mass change matters through the motion present in that mode. **A stationary location contributes no moving-mass effect**.','The changed region can be spring-dominated in one mode and motion-dominated in another. **Stiffness can raise one frequency while inertia lowers the other**.'),
 'air-modes':('The particles move **along the tube**, while the drawn height represents displacement size at each location. The curve is a graph rather than the particles’ literal path.','Neighboring particles can crowd and separate strongly around a small-displacement location. **Compression depends on relative separation, not just local movement size**.'),
 'vowel-shape':('The tongue and lips alter the location and shape of the air passage. **That changes the tract resonances associated with vowel quality**.','One source can be shaped by different tract filters. **Changing the filter changes vowel quality without requiring a new source for each vowel**.'),
 'constriction':('A narrowing changes effective inertia and the restoring response of compressed air. **Both effects must be considered within the mode’s spatial pattern**.','A strong upward shift indicates **a dominant stiffness effect** where compression is important and motion is relatively small for that mode.'),
 'u':('The lip region has strong motion in both first modes. **Inertial loading therefore lowers both F1 and F2** in the /u/ comparison.','Another location can have different roles in the mode patterns. **The word narrowing alone does not determine which effect dominates**.'),
 'i':('The front constriction loads motion in Mode 1 and compression in Mode 2. **F1 falls while F2 rises**.','That location is motion-dominated in the first mode but compression-dominated in the second. **The two modes therefore respond to different dominant effects**.'),
 'a':('At the /a/ location, compression dominates Mode 1 while motion dominates Mode 2. **The stiffness effect raises F1 and the inertial effect lowers F2**.','Moving the constriction changes its position within both mode patterns. **The dominant local roles reverse relative to the /i/ comparison**.'),
 'source':('**F0 determines the spacing of adjacent harmonics**. Harmonics occur at whole-number multiples of the source’s repetition rate.','Greater vocal-fold stiffness supports faster repetition, while greater effective moving mass supports slower repetition. **Those mechanical changes alter F0**.'),
 'filter':('The tract favors harmonics close to its resonances and weakens those farther away. **The resulting envelope carries the formant pattern**.','Pitch is closely related to source repetition, while vowel quality depends strongly on tract resonances. **F0 and the formant pattern describe different contributions**.'),
 'sparse-harmonics':('Large gaps leave fewer harmonic samples near each resonance. **The filter envelope becomes harder to estimate from the available peaks**.','The tract still has a resonant response even if no source harmonic falls close to its maximum. **Poor sampling differs from the absence of a resonance**.'),
 'spectrogram':('It retains the sequence of frequency patterns across analysis windows. **A single spectrum cannot preserve that changing time course**.','**Time is horizontal, frequency vertical and darkness represents amplitude**. Those three visual dimensions should be interpreted separately.'),
 'continuous-speech':('The tract keeps moving between configurations as speech unfolds. **Its changing resonances create moving formant bands**.','Transitions retain information about the changing articulation and neighboring sounds. **A steady middle slice leaves that context out**.'),
 'splice':('The vowel from na contains a transition associated with /n/. **That following information can dominate the identity assigned to the spliced consonant**.','The percept depends on information extending across segments. **Independent classification of each tiny slice leaves out relevant context**.'),
 'vowel-network':('F1 and F2 supply measured features that the learned weights transform into category support. **The five output positions identify the candidate vowels**.','A low F1 and high F2 fit the /i/-like pattern in this example. **Dean is the corresponding correct target**, even if an untrained network currently favors another category.'),
 'weights':('The neuron multiplies each input activation by its connection weight and adds the contributions. **The result is a weighted sum**.','A positive weight preserves an input’s sign and a negative weight reverses it. **Both factors determine the contribution’s direction**.'),
 'forward':('The current input is transformed through successive processing layers using the current weights. **The final result is the network’s prediction**.','The current weights can be poorly learned or untrained. **A correctly executed computation can therefore produce an inaccurate decision**.'),
 'probabilities':('**Entries must be nonnegative and sum to one** across the specified alternatives. A numerical list does not qualify merely because it is an output.','The target identifies the known category, while a valid prediction can favor the wrong one. **Probability validity and accuracy are different tests**.'),
 'backward':('Early contributions depend on downstream computations. **Solving the downstream gradients first makes their results reusable for earlier connections**.','Dynamic programming supplies reuse of dependent calculations, while SGD applies parameter corrections. **Calculating the gradients differs from updating the weights**.'),
 'weight-direction':('Check the incoming sign, the direction it gives the output score and the target’s required change. **Increasing a weight is useful only if its consequence reduces the relevant error**.','Its influence passes through later activations and connections. **Those downstream pathways mediate the final effect**, making the local sign alone insufficient.'),
 'training-data':('The two rows describe the same recording’s measurements and known identity. **Their alignment supplies correct supervision**.','A mismatch associates one recording’s formants with another category. **The update can then teach the wrong input-to-output relationship**.'),
 'sequential':('It specifies that one processing layer’s outputs are passed to the next layer in order. **Adjacent layer widths must agree**.','The new layer must accept what the preceding stage produces and produce what the next expects. **Matching those dimensions preserves a valid computation path**.'),
 'training-code':('The loss measures mismatch, backpropagation calculates gradients and the optimizer applies parameter changes. **These are separate stages of learning**.','Stored gradients can otherwise accumulate across calls. **Clearing them prepares an independent current-step calculation without resetting the learned weights**.'),
 'sigmoid':('Negative sums approach zero, zero maps to one half, and positive sums approach one. **The S-shaped response is bounded and nonlinear**.','Each hidden value is bounded independently, but their total is not constrained. **A category distribution additionally requires a sum of one**.'),
 'sigmoid-flow':('Later layers receive the transformed hidden value as an input. **Their activations and the final decision must be recalculated from it**.','It inserts a nonlinear response between weighted combinations. **The network’s represented function changes even before any parameter update**.'),
 'overlap':('Different labeled vowel tokens can have similar first and second formants. **Those two measurements do not create perfectly isolated category regions**.','The reported accuracy concerns decisions on those particular examples. **Performance on new speakers needs a separate evaluation**.'),
 'accuracy':('Uniform guessing has one correct alternative among five equally likely categories. **Its expected accuracy is twenty percent**.','The measured fraction correct is no longer rising in that run. **A plateau below perfection still includes classification errors**.'),
 'initialization':('Different starting weights create different early predictions and corrections. **That changes the trajectory of learning on the same task**.','The displayed runs can share a final training accuracy despite different routes. **Agreement at the endpoint differs from identical paths**.'),
 'recurrent':('A recurrent connection carries processing state between steps. **Current activity can therefore depend on earlier context**.','The identity or continuation of an item can depend on its sequence. **Processing it alone discards relationships needed for the task**.'),
 'next-token':('The items are represented as ordered vectors and the task predicts a continuation from context. **Their original materials can differ without changing that general organization**.','Context changes which continuations fit and how strongly each is supported. **A distribution can express both restriction and appropriate uncertainty**.'),
 'phonotactics':('The syllable position changes which combinations fit, with onset before the vowel and coda after it. **Allowed sound sequences depend on that structure**.','A boundary can put the consonants into different syllable positions. **A cross-boundary cluster does not have to be a valid single onset**.'),
 'letter-guess':('A beginning limits which completions fit familiar word patterns. **Correct prediction reflects sensitivity to those learned restrictions**.','Some contexts permit many plausible continuations and others permit few. **The distribution should reflect that difference in uncertainty**.'),
 'heads':('Heads contribute alongside one another within a layer, while layers transform representations successively. **Parallel contribution differs from depth**.','A head is part of internal model processing, while an agent is a model assigned a task in a larger system. **The two belong to different levels of organization**.'),
 'dynamic-depth':('The output state of one transformation becomes the input to another. **Repeated change is the useful common relationship**.','Different layers can apply different learned transformations. **The analogy concerns a sequence of states rather than one identical numerical matrix**.'),
 'agents':('The critic’s evaluation returns information that influences another revision. **That feedback links the tasks before the final response**.','A procedure can fail to notice or correct an error. **Correctness still requires evidence about the actual result**, rather than the existence of a checker alone.'),
 'economy':('Both models can express a deviation and relationships that change it over time. **The shared feature is the feedback organization**, not physical material.','The analogy must preserve the causal relationships relevant to the prediction. **Surface resemblance alone does not transfer a mechanism**.'),
 'speech':('Speech coordinates complex hidden articulatory movements with little direct visual feedback or explicit instruction. **That coordination develops before the instruction-heavy skills of reading and writing**.','It studies **how the speech organs move and configure the tract**. Those physical actions supply the articulatory description of a sound.'),
 'acoustics':('Tract movements shape the passage containing vibrating air, changing the resulting sound. **Acoustic phonetics studies that sound and its relationship to production**.','Articulation describes organ configurations and movements, while acoustics describes the resulting signal. **They are linked stages with different measurements**.'),
 'ai-science':('A convincing response is observed behavior, not a complete mechanism. **Its explanation needs evidence about the processing that produced it**.','A testable account connects specified inputs, operations and representations with an observable result. **Different mechanisms can then be compared against evidence**.'),
 'reasoning':('Applying an idea requires using its relationships in a changed case. **Recalling a phrase alone does not establish that ability**.','Different-looking objects can preserve the same relevant causal relationship. **Identifying that relationship makes the comparison useful**.'),
 'fricatives':('The constriction can remain in the same place while vocal-fold vibration changes. **/f/ and /v/ share place and manner but differ in voicing**.','Dental fricatives narrow at the teeth, while postalveolar fricatives narrow farther back. **The location of articulation changes**, independently of whether the sound is voiced.'),
 'stops':('Both close the mouth, but a nasal stop permits airflow through a lowered velum into the nose. **An oral stop blocks that nasal route**.','Both are voiced labial stops. **/m/ has nasal airflow because the velum is lowered**, while /b/ uses an oral release.'),
 'consonants':('Voicing concerns vocal-fold vibration, place concerns the constriction location and manner concerns its type. **They supply distinct physical dimensions**.','The sounds share voiced alveolar closure but differ in the nasal route. **Stating both agreement and difference gives a complete physical comparison**.'),
 'ai-skills':('Recognition uses current representations to identify an input, while learning changes those representations. **Using knowledge differs from acquiring it**.','It can preserve selected functional relationships while simplifying the implementation. **A useful model does not require literal biological identity**.'),
 'closure':('The available marks can support a coherent whole even without complete edges. **Closure supplies organization beyond the isolated fragments**.','A cloze task withholds part of a sequence and asks for a fitting completion. **The surrounding relationships constrain the missing part**.'),
 'completion':('A suitable answer must fit regularities in the supplied context. **Successful completion therefore expresses useful learned relationships**.','The surrounding items limit which continuations make sense. **Their relationships provide information that an isolated missing slot lacks**.'),
 'learning':('Random parameters can still be used to calculate a response. **Producing a guess does not mean the weights already encode useful knowledge**.','The prediction must be compared with a training objective and used to change the parameters. **An unchanged repeated calculation alone does not teach the target relationship**.'),
 'sgd':('The sign of the discrepancy determines whether the correction goes up or down. **Subtracting a fraction of it moves the estimate toward the sampled value**.','Different sampled observations pull in different directions. **Local fluctuation can coexist with an overall tendency toward the data’s average**.'),
 'initial-estimate':('The starting estimate is an initial condition, while the target is supported by the observations. **Changing the start need not change the target**.','A guess above the target improves by moving down, while one below improves by moving up. **Improvement concerns a smaller discrepancy, not one fixed numerical direction**.'),
 'sgd-down':('The discrepancy is positive when the estimate exceeds the observation. **Subtracting part of it lowers the estimate toward that observation**.','The learning rate scales the correction to a fraction. **The new estimate therefore retains some of its previous value** rather than being replaced by the observation.'),
 'sgd-up':('The discrepancy is negative when the observation exceeds the estimate. **Subtracting a fraction of a negative quantity raises the estimate**.','Upward movement can bring a low estimate closer to the data. **The estimate’s direction and the error’s direction are different descriptions**.'),
 'rate':('A larger rate makes each observation produce a bigger correction. **It increases adjustment speed and the influence of sample variation**.','A positive small rate still applies corrections. **Learning continues with smaller steps**, usually producing slower and steadier movement in the example.'),
 'system':('Relationships determine how one element’s state affects another and how the whole behavior develops. **A parts list leaves out that organization**.','It links a current state to its direction and rate of change. **Following the rule explains a trajectory through time**.'),
 'octopus':('The arms must coordinate with one another, the surface and the target. **The useful action depends on the interaction**, not an isolated arm movement.','Both coordinate many moving parts around an action. **The organization of the parts is the shared relationship**, despite different organs and goals.'),
 'greedy':('An inexpensive edge can lead into a costly remainder. **Immediate cost is different from complete-path cost**.','It gains speed by making limited local comparisons. **It can sacrifice the globally best answer** by ignoring later consequences.'),
 'exhaustive':('It evaluates every complete candidate and compares their total costs. **The best finite candidate is not omitted**.','Overlapping routes contain shared continuations that are recalculated separately. **That repeated work makes the search expensive**.'),
 'dynamic-programming':('It stores the best continuation from a shared state and reuses it. **Every earlier path needing that remainder can use the solved value**.','A larger problem requires the answers of its dependent smaller problems. **Solving those dependencies first makes the needed values available**.'),
 'value':('It summarizes the **best complete continuation from the current state to the goal**. It is more than one edge’s cost.','The sum includes both the next step and the optimal remaining route. **The immediate edge alone leaves future costs out**.'),
 'least-time':('Different regions can have different travel speeds. **A longer route through faster material can take less time**.','Different objectives can favor different routes. **The answer depends on whether distance, time or another quantity is minimized**.'),
 'settling':('The change points against the displacement, reducing the gap from equilibrium. **The correction shrinks as the deviation shrinks**.','A return direction alone does not account for carrying motion past the target. **Inertia supplies the continued motion needed for repeated overshoot**.'),
 'position-velocity':('Zero position identifies equilibrium, not zero motion. **A moving mass can pass through the center with substantial velocity**.','A turning point has momentarily zero velocity away from equilibrium. **At an equilibrium passage, position is zero while motion continues**.'),
 'frequency':('Frequency counts cycles per unit time, while amplitude measures movement size. **Fast repetition and large displacement are independent descriptions**.','A longer recording can contain more cycles without a faster vibration. **The interval must be fixed to compare cycle rates**.'),
 'cochlea':('Light, stiff regions respond best to high frequencies, while heavier, more compliant regions respond best to low ones. **The mechanical gradient separates the mixture**.','Different responding locations activate associated neural pathways. **Place provides information about which frequencies were present**.'),
 'euler':('It uses a state and its change rule to calculate a nearby next state. **Many small steps approximate the continuous trajectory**.','Using a new position rather than the old one changes the values entering the velocity update. **That change defines a different numerical procedure**.'),
 'templates':('A new input is compared with learned patterns, and a good match supports recognition. **Prior experience supplies the stored comparison**.','It combines corresponding entries into a comparison score. **The score reflects the relationship between the two numerical patterns**.'),
 'hierarchy':('Each stage transforms the representation available to the next. **The final decision depends on these successive computations**.','They lie between the supplied input and the final labeled output. **Hidden names their internal processing role**, not an additional category.'),
 'brain-model':('It keeps selected relationships among incoming activity, connection strengths and a response. **It simplifies the biological implementation**.','An abstract functional relationship can be useful without reproducing all physical details. **The model’s behavior needs its own evidence**.'),
 'bad-data':('The update responds to the data it receives, including erroneous observations. **It can correctly execute a correction toward a corrupted target**.','A valid algorithm can still receive misleading inputs. **Data quality and update correctness are separate questions**.'),
 'air-pressure':('Particles alternately crowd together and separate, changing density and pressure. **Those local changes form the propagating sound pattern**.','A particle oscillates locally while the disturbance travels through the medium. **The signal’s travel is not the particle’s full journey**.'),
 'waveform':('It records the changing value of a quantity such as pressure at one location. **A repeated trace represents cycles through time**.','A time trace follows one location across moments, while a mode drawing compares positions at a stage of the motion. **Their horizontal axes have different meanings**.'),
 'mixture':('Several component vibrations contribute simultaneously to the recorded signal. **The waveform reflects their combined motion**.','It separates the contributions by frequency and relative amplitude. **Different mixtures can have different qualities even when some frequencies are shared**.'),
 'inertia':('The mass has velocity as it reaches equilibrium and continues moving. **Being at the middle does not itself remove that motion**.','The spring supplies a restoring force, while mass resists changes in motion. **Their interaction produces the overshoot and reversal**.'),
 'differential':('It states how a present quantity determines a rate of change. **Following that relationship predicts the system’s behavior over time**.','A sign gives a direction such as return or departure from equilibrium. **That conceptual relationship differs from a memorized list of numerical updates**.'),
 'recognition':('The input represents measured information, while the output represents support for possible identities. **They have different interpretive roles**.','Different weights assign different influences to the same measurements. **A new decision can follow from a changed learned mapping**.'),
 'network-shape':('There are **three hidden layers**, containing three, two and four neurons. The final five-neuron layer is the output.','The number of incoming weights equals the number of neurons in the preceding fully connected layer. **Each incoming value has its own connection weight**.'),
 'levels':('A neuron combines inputs, a network combines processing stages and an agentic system connects task-performing models. **They describe different levels of organization**.','The higher organization is built from the lower computations. **A larger system still relies on the weighted transformations performed inside its models**.'),
 'atomic-analogy':('It can transfer the idea of organized wave patterns and characteristic modes. **It does not make the compared objects physically identical**.','An analogy preserves selected relevant relationships rather than every detail. **A familiar picture is not automatically a literal account of the underlying physics**.'),
 'software':('Explicit procedures state operations, learned parameters encode relationships from examples, and communicating models organize connected tasks. **The categories distinguish how task behavior is supplied**.','An agentic arrangement can use trained models that run through executable programs. **The three forms can therefore contribute to one system together**.'),
 'learned-knowledge':('Their collective values encode relationships used to process an input and support a prediction. **Training changes those learned relationships**.','The input describes the current case, while the weights supply the learned processing. **Either can change a response for a different reason**.'),
 'connection-scale':('A useful decision can depend on many interacting connections rather than one isolated stored fact. **Both examples motivate a distributed organization of knowledge**.','A large count does not establish identical processing. **Mechanisms must be compared through the relationships and behavior they support**.'),
 'two-vibrators':('The vocal folds supply the driving vibration and the tract’s air supplies a shaped physical response. **Both contribute to voiced speech in different roles**.','Tongue and lip movement change the air passage without requiring another vocal-fold source. **The air’s response can change while the source continues**.')
}
